------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAP (components/ui/Modal.tsx → native) — each rule unit-asserted
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  open / onClose / title / size / children / ariaLabel        → all reproduced.
  size sm|md|lg|full → max-w 384 / 512 / 672 / min(96%,1100)  → ModalAdapter.maxWidth(for:in:).
  `< sm` (640) full-screen sheet vs `sm:` centered card        → isCompact / pinsToBottom / resolvedWidth.
  `rounded-none` mobile vs `sm:rounded-lg`                      → ModalAdapter.cornerRadii (top-only vs all).
  `max-h-[100dvh]` vs `sm:max-h-[90vh]`                         → ModalAdapter.maxHeightFraction (1.0 / 0.9).
  `h-11 w-11` close (WCAG 2.5.5)                                → ModalAdapter.closeButtonSide == 44.
  `aria-labelledby` (title) vs `aria-label` (ariaLabel)        → ModalProjection.resolveLabel → .titled/.anonymous/.untitled.
  `title && (<header/>)`                                        → ModalProjection.showsHeader.
  backdrop onClick / Esc / (native) swipe-down                 → scrim tap · macOS onExitCommand · DragGesture.
  `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"`                        → .accessibilityAddTraits(.isModal) + label + .escape action.
  arbitrary `children` (any load state)                        → ModalProjection.resolvePhase (loading/empty/error/data).

  STATES (all render real chrome — never a blank box): loading (skeleton), empty (ContentUnavailableView),
  error (retry), stale (chip + reconnecting banner + one auto-refresh), offline (chip + cached banner),
  data (caller content). Map: web Recharts→Swift Charts / web Leaflet→MapKit — N/A (source has none).

